IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Asbestos-related Claims (Management of Commonwealth Liabilities) Act 2005
-- (Cth) — THE NOUNS, THE RULES AND THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL. Source:
-- ../registers/source-bundle/C2005A00122.txt (compilation of 1 July 2014).
-- Part 2 commenced on 26 October 2005. The person with an asbestos-related
-- condition asks: "Is mine an asbestos-related claim under the Act; may I
-- claim against Comcare; who is liable to me now?"

§ `Nouns`

-- s 3(1) asbestos-related condition.
DECLARE `Condition` IS ONE OF
    `asbestosis`
    `an asbestos-induced carcinoma`
    `an asbestos-related non-malignant pleural disease`
    `mesothelioma`
    `another condition caused by exposure to asbestos`
    `a condition not caused by asbestos`

-- s 3(1): who breached the duty of care, as at the breach.
DECLARE `Who breached the duty` IS ONE OF
    `the Commonwealth`
    `a Commonwealth authority at the time of the breach`
    `Comcare, Australia Post, Telstra, a body declared not to be an authority, or their subsidiary`
    `someone else`

-- s 3(1) liability (a)-(c): what the liability arises under.
DECLARE `Source of liability` IS ONE OF
    `the breach of duty, not yet settled or finally decided`
    `a contract of insurance`
    `a judgment not stayed or under appeal on 26 October 2005`
    `a written settlement made before 26 October 2005`

-- s 5: against whom I made the claim.
DECLARE `Claim made against` IS ONE OF
    `the Commonwealth or the authority`
    `Comcare`
    `no one yet`

DECLARE `Liable party` IS ONE OF
    `Comcare`
    `the authority or its successor, after the Minister's declaration`
    `the Commonwealth or the authority, as before`
    `not affected by this Act`

DECLARE `Asbestos case` HAS
    `my condition`                                          IS A `Condition`
    `who breached the duty`                                 IS A `Who breached the duty`
    `the liability arises under`                            IS A `Source of liability`
    `I claimed against`                                     IS A `Claim made against`
    `I made the claim on`                                   IS A DATE
    -- s 6
    `the Minister declared the liability transferred back`  IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Asbestos position` HAS
    `mine is an asbestos-related claim`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `I may claim against Comcare`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `who is liable to me`                                   IS A `Liable party`
    `the liability passed to Comcare on`                    IS A MAYBE DATE

§ `Rules`

`the commencement of Part 2` MEANS Date 26 10 2005

-- s 3(1) asbestos-related claim: compensation or damages for an
-- asbestos-related condition from a breach of duty of care by the Commonwealth
-- or an entity that was a Commonwealth authority when the breach occurred.
@ref s 3(1)
GIVEN c IS A `Asbestos case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is an asbestos-related claim` c IF
        NOT (c's `my condition` EQUALS `a condition not caused by asbestos`)
    AND (   c's `who breached the duty` EQUALS `the Commonwealth`
         OR c's `who breached the duty` EQUALS `a Commonwealth authority at the time of the breach`)

-- s 3(1) liability: not under an insurance contract, a final judgment, or a
-- written settlement before Part 2 commenced.
@ref s 3(1) liability
GIVEN c IS A `Asbestos case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act transfers the liability` c IF
        `it is an asbestos-related claim` c
    AND c's `the liability arises under` EQUALS `the breach of duty, not yet settled or finally decided`

-- s 5(3): from commencement, anyone who could make an asbestos-related claim
-- against the Commonwealth or an authority may claim against Comcare, whatever
-- the source of the liability (changed after the independent pass).
@ref s 5(3)(a)
GIVEN c IS A `Asbestos case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I may claim against Comcare` c IF `it is an asbestos-related claim` c

-- s 5(1): claims made against the Commonwealth or an authority on or before
-- commencement pass on commencement; a claim against Comcare before then does
-- not (changed after the independent pass). s 5(2), (3)(b): later claims pass
-- when made.
@ref s 5
GIVEN c IS A `Asbestos case`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the transfer day for` c MEANS
    IF (NOT (`the Act transfers the liability` c)) OR c's `I claimed against` EQUALS `no one yet`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF c's `I made the claim on` AT MOST `the commencement of Part 2`
         THEN IF c's `I claimed against` EQUALS `the Commonwealth or the authority`
              THEN JUST `the commencement of Part 2`
              ELSE NOTHING
         ELSE JUST (c's `I made the claim on`)

-- s 6: the Minister may transfer an authority's (not the Commonwealth's)
-- liability back to the authority or its successor.
@ref ss 5-6
GIVEN c IS A `Asbestos case`
GIVETH A `Liable party`
`who is liable for` c MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the Act transfers the liability` c) THEN `not affected by this Act`
        IF `the transfer day for` c EQUALS NOTHING THEN `the Commonwealth or the authority, as before`
        IF     c's `who breached the duty` EQUALS `a Commonwealth authority at the time of the breach`
           AND c's `the Minister declared the liability transferred back`
            THEN `the authority or its successor, after the Minister's declaration`
        OTHERWISE `Comcare`

@ref ss 3, 5, 6
@export default The position of a person with an asbestos-related condition under the Asbestos-related Claims (Management of Commonwealth Liabilities) Act 2005 (Cth): whether their claim is an asbestos-related claim (asbestosis, asbestos-induced carcinoma, non-malignant pleural disease, mesothelioma or another asbestos condition, from a breach of duty of care by the Commonwealth or an entity that was then a Commonwealth authority: s 3); whether they may claim against Comcare (s 5(3)); who is liable to them (Comcare, from 26 October 2005 for earlier claims or from when a later claim is made, unless the Minister has transferred an authority's liability back: ss 5-6); liabilities under insurance contracts, final judgments or earlier written settlements are not affected. DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Asbestos case`  @desc My condition, who breached the duty, what the liability arises under, my claim and its date, and any ministerial declaration
GIVETH A `Asbestos position`
`the asbestos position for` c MEANS
    `Asbestos position` OF `it is an asbestos-related claim` c, `I may claim against Comcare` c, `who is liable for` c, `the transfer day for` c
